From 5a8297caf55347a4a132452737978c88ba907def Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: graham <grahamseamans@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:10:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add transfer-impedance interface layers to the coupled
 FEM-BEM core

A thin locally reacting layer on a FEM-BEM interface turns the collocated
continuity row p_F - p_B = 0 into p_F - p_B = Z_s v_n, with
Z_s = R + time_derivative(omega) M and v_n along the bounded region's
outward normal. With q = neumann_scale * v_n this is one diagonal entry
-d, d = Z_s / neumann_scale, per interface dof on the flux-flux block.

- interface_transfer_impedance_jump_coefficients builds the block once;
  host monolithic, CUDA/ROCm (sparse scatter) and condensed :none and
  :pressure consume it. :pressure substitutes p_Gamma = P p_B + D q in
  the Schur and mechanical rows and in the retained-pressure recovery.
- :flux elimination refuses under on and falls back to :pressure under
  auto; the speaker ROM and the interior-only solve refuse.
- Wire: boundary.parameters["transfer_impedance"] = {model:
  "resistance_mass", resistance_pa_s_per_m, mass_kg_per_m2} on the
  interface's bounded boundary, validated strictly.
- pressure_continuity_error is the residual of the interface condition;
  interface_transfer_impedance diagnostics record R, M and Z_s.
- An absent layer or R = M = 0 exactly writes nothing: results are
  bit-identical to v0.3.0.

